{"id":"99a24a38-defc-4109-8348-35c72a77479f","finding_id":null,"source":"odc","issue_type":"sca","repo_url":null,"base_ref":null,"rule_id":null,"cve_id":"CVE-2019-25225","ghsa_id":"GHSA-QHXP-V273-G94H","cwe":[{"id":"CWE-79","name":null}],"owasp":[],"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":null,"file_path":"scan/package-lock.json?/sanitize-html:1.4.2","line_range":null,"package_name":"sanitize-html","package_version":"1.4.2","fixed_version":null,"purl":"pkg:npm/sanitize-html@1.4.2","ecosystem":"npm","message":"`sanitize-html` prior to version 2.0.0-beta is vulnerable to Cross-site Scripting (XSS). The `sanitizeHtml()` function in `index.js` does not sanitize content when using the custom `transformTags` option, which is intended to convert attribute values into text. As a result, malicious input can be transformed into executable code.","finding_url":null,"dataflow_trace":null,"validation_profile":null,"raw_payload":{"fileName":"sanitize-html:1.4.2","filePath":"/scan/package-lock.json?/sanitize-html:1.4.2","vulnerability":{"source":"NPM","name":"GHSA-qhxp-v273-g94h","unscored":"true","severity":"moderate","cvssv3":{"baseScore":6.099999904632568,"attackVector":"NETWORK","attackComplexity":"LOW","privilegesRequired":"NONE","userInteraction":"REQUIRED","scope":"CHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"LOW","integrityImpact":"LOW","availabilityImpact":"NONE","baseSeverity":"MEDIUM","version":"3.1"},"cwes":["CWE-79"],"description":"`sanitize-html` prior to version 2.0.0-beta is vulnerable to Cross-site Scripting (XSS). The `sanitizeHtml()` function in `index.js` does not sanitize content when using the custom `transformTags` option, which is intended to convert attribute values into text. As a result, malicious input can be transformed into executable code.","notes":"","references":[{"source":"NPM Advisory reference: ","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2019-25225","name":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2019-25225"},{"source":"NPM Advisory reference: ","url":"https://gith